# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What must never leave this machine.
#
# This repo holds the INSTRUMENT (questionnaire source, build scripts, do-files,
# checks). It does not hold data or literature. Three reasons, in order of how
# badly each would go wrong:
#
#   1. Licensed microdata. VASyR (UNHCR), STEP (World Bank) and the Philippines
#      STEP household file are redistributable only under their own terms, which
#      a GitHub repo does not satisfy.
#   2. Real respondent data. The 46-person pilot is field data about identifiable
#      people in a small population; a private repo is not a safeguard.
#   3. Copyrighted papers. ~220 MB of PDFs and their text extractions.
#
# Anything genuinely public (HCES government material) is excluded too, simply
# because it is large and re-downloadable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- licensed microdata ---
microdata/

# --- real respondent data (the 46-person pilot) ---
pilot/

# --- literature: papers and their extractions ---
literature/

# --- generated datasets. The pipeline rebuilds all of these from source. ---
*.dta
*.csv
*.log
*.smcl
*.rtf
replication/final_instrument/data/
replication/*.dta
replication/*.log

# --- build artefacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.aux
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
~$*
*.tmp

# --- local editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.lnk

# --- downloaded journal article and literature note-extractions ---
# (the four lines above now cover everything that used to be listed here)
